cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use AutoFL in your research, please cite both the paper and this
  software artifact.
title: "AutoFL: System and Benchmark Suite"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chiu
    given-names: Yen-Jung
    affiliation: "Department of Biomedical Engineering, Chang Gung University, Taoyuan, Taiwan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2087-2266"
abstract: >-
  AutoFL converts existing machine-learning training scripts into
  federated-learning (FL) client modules. This artifact contains the AutoFL
  source code (AST rewriter, LLM-based converter, five-stage preflight
  validator, sample-weighted FedAvg runtime), five conversion strategies
  (AST rewriting, a rule-based template converter, and zero-shot, few-shot,
  and schema-augmented LLM prompting), the 13-script benchmark suite spanning
  PyTorch, TensorFlow, PyTorch Lightning, MONAI, scikit-learn, and XGBoost,
  a frozen 33-script expansion benchmark, and the generated client files of
  every experiment.
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - prompt engineering
  - large language models
  - code generation
  - FedAvg
  - benchmark
